# Line endings are a correctness concern here, not a style preference.
#
# scripts/backup.sh shipped with CRLF. On the Linux VPS the runbook targets,
# both invocation paths died before doing any work:
#   ./scripts/backup.sh  -> env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#   bash scripts/backup.sh -> set: pipefail: invalid option name  (exit 2)
# `set` is a special builtin, so its failure aborts the script outright — the
# backup silently never ran and -e/-u/pipefail never activated.
#
# The frozen-artifact model is the second reason. Issue HTML is hashed and the
# archive signature is bound to those bytes, so a CRLF checkout of the MJML
# templates would freeze a different htmlSha256 than an LF checkout of the same
# commit. Pinning eol=lf keeps the artifact hash a property of the commit.

# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where a stray CR is a runtime failure rather
# than a cosmetic diff.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
